    "body": "agent-note:v1 — salvage note (duplicate-record disposition, task 13783)\n- PR #7864 is the canonical artifact for task 13783 / issue #5854: its record doc/2026-11-08_decision_id5854_per_target_composition.md (74f87b8f3e, refined dc712e6e2b) was committed first and this PR was opened for it.\n- Concurrent claims of task 13783 (lane code-h and the session working this branch) produced a second, competing record from lane code-h: doc/2026-11-08_decision_id5854_per_target_customisation_system.md (f91d3f043d, 547 lines), briefly pushed onto this branch. It has been removed by revert d9d763c296; this PR now contains only the canonical record. No force push was used.\n- Salvage diff (code-h record vs canonical, read in full): the canonical record covers every acceptance bullet for #5854 — cascade, themes, override maps, asset substitution, conditional blocks, the worked three-target example, invariants, alternatives, sibling dependencies (#5849-#5855 named), and the no-parent-change statement. Nothing required is unique to the removed record. Three points were alternative rulings, not gaps, and are recorded here in case a future amendment wants them: (1) presentation selection modelled as strictly separate from the property cascade, with raw CSS explicitly barred from affecting presentation selection (canonical: one ladder, presentation overrides at layer 4, raw CSS at layer 5 restricted to presentation properties); (2) a missing substituted content asset falling back to the base asset with a warning (canonical §4: missing asset at build time is an error for theme/content mechanisms); (3) a sparseness warning when a per-target theme delta redefines nearly every token (canonical: base → target → mode-variant theme layering without a delta-sparseness rule).\n- Lane code-h parks its queue claim on task 13783 naming this PR as the active artifact; the session driving PR #7864 continues to its disposition.\n",
